  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U12U-READ-1",
      "title": "My Aunt the Nurse",
      "text": "My aunt works as a nurse in a small hospital. Her schedule is full: she works ten hours a day and often has no time for lunch. Last week a woman with cancer came to her floor. The woman had to take five pills every morning, and her son had to fill out many forms at the front desk. My aunt helped him find out where to pay. On Friday the hospital canceled a big meeting because a fire alarm went off. Nobody knew how it occurred, but everyone had to escape down the stairs in one minute. My aunt was the last one out. She says the job is hard, but it fulfills her dream of helping people. The waiting room is always filled with worried faces, and she supports them with a smile."
    }
  ],
